WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.929
- I just wanted to do right, by her,

00:00:04.929 --> 00:00:07.857
because I am still here.

00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:16.570
My sister's name is Heather.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.290
She passed away from pancreatic cancer.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:21.269
- I lost my brother on my tenth birthday.

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:23.066
- I lost my brother to suicide

00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:24.209
and his name was Harry.

00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:27.194
- I lost my brother
when he was 16 years old

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:28.133
in a car accident.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.339
- I have a lot of memories
of him just tickling me,

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:32.511
so hard, that I couldn't breathe.

00:00:32.511 --> 00:00:34.751
- She was sarcastic and sassy

00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:38.265
and the smartest person
that I might ever know.

00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:40.280
- His friends are still
in contact with me today

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.545
and every time they see me,

00:00:41.545 --> 00:00:43.461
they tell me how much I look like him.

00:00:43.461 --> 00:00:44.471
- When I think about him,

00:00:44.471 --> 00:00:45.548
I think of him as he was,

00:00:45.548 --> 00:00:46.685
which is like a teenager.

00:00:46.685 --> 00:00:48.521
And then when I dream about him,

00:00:48.521 --> 00:00:50.932
he's almost always like a baby.

00:00:50.932 --> 00:00:51.887
Whenever he's in my dreams,

00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:54.765
I'll like pick him up and just hold him.

00:00:54.765 --> 00:00:56.070
It's really nice.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.524
- We found out during my birthday party,

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.726
that he was found dead.

00:01:01.726 --> 00:01:02.753
- I looked down at my phone

00:01:02.753 --> 00:01:05.006
and my little sister had just called

00:01:05.006 --> 00:01:05.912
and it's kind of one of those things

00:01:05.912 --> 00:01:06.690
that you can't describe

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.231
but you just know.

00:01:08.231 --> 00:01:10.173
- He and my grandmother decided to

00:01:10.173 --> 00:01:11.333
take a road trip together.

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:14.085
I remember very vividly
seeing my grandfather

00:01:14.085 --> 00:01:17.019
and the police officer
walk through my back door.

00:01:17.019 --> 00:01:18.067
- It happened about a year ago

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.867
and I got a message from him

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:21.690
and made the decision to drive home.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.513
So, I got to see him that night

00:01:23.513 --> 00:01:25.230
and then it happened the next morning.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.450
- I called my sister back

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:31.450
and she let me know
that Heather was, gone.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.729
- And it was just the hardest thing,

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:35.545
to watch my mom,

00:01:35.545 --> 00:01:38.515
her being in bed and
just crying and crying.

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:40.311
- And my grandfather just said,

00:01:40.311 --> 00:01:42.506
"There was an accident in Nevada."

00:01:42.506 --> 00:01:44.791
- My initial instinct was to,

00:01:44.791 --> 00:01:46.547
want to talk to her immediately

00:01:46.547 --> 00:01:48.706
and I can't tell you how many times

00:01:48.706 --> 00:01:49.854
I actually took to the phone

00:01:49.854 --> 00:01:51.240
and went, "Oh no,

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.233
"that number doesn't work anymore."

00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:55.986
- It's been over a year

00:01:55.986 --> 00:01:57.274
but it doesn't feel like over a year.

00:01:57.274 --> 00:01:59.292
It feels like yesterday, you know.

00:01:59.292 --> 00:02:01.547
- It took me a long time
to stop entertaining

00:02:01.547 --> 00:02:03.195
the thought that maybe it wasn't real.

00:02:03.195 --> 00:02:04.692
- There's always the questions of like,

00:02:04.692 --> 00:02:05.831
"Well, if I was home.

00:02:05.831 --> 00:02:07.493
"If I was closer.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.325
"Would I have been able to do anything?"

00:02:09.325 --> 00:02:11.957
- There are moments that you are so fine

00:02:11.957 --> 00:02:13.213
and then the next second,

00:02:13.213 --> 00:02:17.916
for no reason, you're like
a crying heap on the floor.

00:02:17.916 --> 00:02:21.251
- When I feel myself
go into the pain of it,

00:02:21.251 --> 00:02:24.172
I allow myself to because I
think that that's important.

00:02:24.172 --> 00:02:25.334
- It doesn't matter how much I heal

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.377
or how much emotional
processing I go through.

00:02:27.377 --> 00:02:28.875
How much I pray or go to therapy,

00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:30.592
or whatever, he's still gone.

00:02:30.592 --> 00:02:33.019
- You wait for that sadness to go away,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:33.831
like it won't.

00:02:33.831 --> 00:02:36.653
- I think the only way to
make it completely go away

00:02:36.653 --> 00:02:39.496
would be to forget about him.

00:02:39.496 --> 00:02:41.530
- I know this is cliche but honestly,

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:42.794
I think about him everyday.

00:02:42.794 --> 00:02:44.175
- There's not a day, that goes by,

00:02:44.175 --> 00:02:45.680
that I don't think about her.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.734
- I don't know that it will
really ever feel normal

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.333
because, I mean it can't.

00:02:51.333 --> 00:02:53.261
- That sort of empty space in my life,

00:02:53.261 --> 00:02:55.340
it's still there, it's
still an empty space,

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.439
but it doesn't feel so glaring, anymore.

00:02:58.439 --> 00:03:01.980
- It's like a heavy, heavy weight

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.720
but maybe the weight is still heavy

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.077
and I just have gotten stronger.

00:03:06.077 --> 00:03:10.037
- It doesn't get easier.

00:03:12.277 --> 00:03:13.741
It get's more manageable.

